  "sheets": [
    {
      "id": "parts",
      "size": "1536x1024",
      "prompt": "Image 1 is a sticker of a duckling character. Draw this exact duckling as a cut-out paper puppet: its separate body parts laid out on one sheet, the same drawing style, colours, texture, line and proportions as in image 1, every part at the size it has in image 1.\n\nDraw each part on its own, spread out over the sheet with wide empty gaps between them, no part touching or overlapping another:\n1. the body: the fluffy yellow body with its tail fluff, facing right as in image 1, without head, without feet and WITHOUT ANY WING: where the near wing lies against the body in image 1, draw only plain fluffy yellow body feathers, no wing shape and no wing outline on it; its top, normally under the head, rounded.\n2. the head: the round fluffy yellow head, facing right as in image 1, with a completely blank face — no eye, no beak — keep the rosy cheek; its bottom edge rounded.\n3. the wing: the small fluffy near wing folded as in image 1, with a rounded shoulder.\n4. the open wing: the same small wing spread out, flapping, with a rounded shoulder.\n5. one foot: an orange webbed foot with its short leg.\n\nEvery part is drawn whole, including what is normally hidden behind another part, and each joint end (where it tucks under the body or the head) is a full, smooth, rounded edge. No text, no labels, no numbers, no outline around the parts beyond the drawing's own line, no shadows. Fully transparent background."
    },
    {
      "id": "face",
      "size": "1536x1024",
      "references": [
        "parts"
      ],
      "prompt": "Image 1 is a sticker of a duckling character; image 2 shows the same duckling cut into puppet parts, with a blank face. Draw the duckling's face pieces as separate stickers on one sheet: the same drawing style, colours and line as in image 1, every piece at the size it has on the duckling in image 1, so it fits the blank face in image 2.\n\nDraw each piece on its own, spread out in tidy rows with wide empty gaps between them, nothing touching:\n1. the duckling's eye as it is in image 1: a dark round eye with a white sparkle.\n2. the same eye wide open and surprised: bigger and rounder, with its white sparkle.\n3. the same eye gently closed in sleep: a soft downward-curving line with a few lashes.\n4. the same eye closed in a happy smile: an upward-curving arc.\n5. the same eye sad: looking down, its upper lid tilted up towards the middle.\n6. the beak as it is in image 1: the flat orange beak, closed.\n7. the beak wide open, quacking.\n8. the beak a little open.\n\nNo text, no labels, no numbers, no shadows, no face or head around the pieces. Fully transparent background."
    }
